  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{0, 0}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,ExpressionUUID->"b67233a5-792b-4139-9d79-cef9bcd5b5c2"],

Cell["1. What is a cartogram?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8d7d58db-7d2f-4d2d-9282-33cc904668dc"],

Cell["\<\
A geographic map of the world devotes enormous screen area to Russia, Canada, \
and the Sahara, and a few pixels each to Bangladesh, South Korea, or the \
Netherlands. If the question being asked is \"where do people live?\" or \
\"where is the economy?\", this is the opposite of what we want. \
Density-equalising cartograms solve this by reshaping each region so that its \
area tells the story of a variable of interest.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8a780dc4-d7bc-424e-8314-ae0d7e19987b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Gastner & Newman's elegant insight (PNAS 2004) is that a map in which \
density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", 
    StyleBox["r",
     FontWeight->Bold], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "bc770952-169a-4293-adae-2d93b1b45a89"],
 " is uniform is exactly what we want, and diffusion is the natural process \
that takes any non-uniform density to a uniform one. We therefore simulate \
the heat equation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ffcea8c-42da-48e3-8dd5-21c11e72a477"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", 
     StyleBox["r",
      FontWeight->Bold], ",", " ", "t", ")"}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[Del]", "2"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", 
     StyleBox["r",
      FontWeight->Bold], ",", " ", "t", ")"}]}], ",", 
   "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n",
     FontWeight->Bold], "\[CenterDot]", "\[Del]", "\[Rho]"}], "=", "0", ",", 
   "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", "on", "\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"e8949e6b-7f1d-4eae-a86d-c8f92641b261"],

Cell["\<\
on a rectangular domain with Neumann boundary conditions (no flux through the \
box edge, so mass is conserved), and flow each geographic point through the \
instantaneous velocity\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0d2c1647-a9e5-44b5-8ddd-231f191c0c49"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"d", " ", 
     StyleBox["r",
      FontWeight->Bold]}], 
    RowBox[{"d", " ", "t"}]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["v",
     FontWeight->Bold], "(", 
    StyleBox["r",
     FontWeight->Bold], ",", " ", "t", ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Del]", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", 
       StyleBox["r",
        FontWeight->Bold], ",", " ", "t", ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", 
      StyleBox["r",
       FontWeight->Bold], ",", " ", "t", ")"}]]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"4a192539-3f2f-457b-b1b2-17c51c8a5449"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"t", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "26a0846d-1d3c-4760-91cc-844821cd1fa7"],
 " the density relaxes to its spatial mean and the advected points settle \
into their cartogram positions. Regions of high initial density draw space \
inwards and therefore expand; regions of low density are pushed outwards."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"62d1ce77-c74d-4897-bf73-ace2d0079e87"],

Cell["2. The algorithm, step by step", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dd7d8f9a-47f2-4ddc-a060-b627fcbad527"],

Cell["2.1 Rasterise polygons to a density grid", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fac10760-8738-4ce2-b9c8-11015baecf36"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Given a collection of country polygons and a per-country metric ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["M", "c"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ff1f278c-021f-49d0-b35a-339ac686a519"],
 " (population, GDP, \[Ellipsis]), we set the density inside polygon ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["c", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "71590194-4872-4ebb-9023-64a2a9172665"],
 " to"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"60b67c79-9a10-48bc-9c45-5ccbb90b06bc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "0"], "(", 
    StyleBox["r",
     FontWeight->Bold], ")"}], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox["M", "c"], 
    SubscriptBox["A", "c"]], ",", "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", "for", "\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["r",
     FontWeight->Bold], "\[Element]", "c"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"002da059-3bc2-4400-836f-72d0ac808e4d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", "c"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "b20392b6-c7eb-426e-9646-30dab51c7f50"],
 " is the geographic area of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["c", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "811968a6-2ba4-49ec-819e-83978c334fc2"],
 ". Integrated over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["c", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "9993130a-0c9a-4061-8b14-8bff4ad7a9e3"],
 " we recover the metric ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["M", "c"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "1e41fc59-5c65-438c-b0e1-91499885b6e5"],
 ". Ocean cells are filled with the mean land density so the spatial mean is \
uniform across the domain and oceans retain their size; only the relative \
sizes of countries change."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5ee2afaa-d7cc-46f7-95a8-c47fcc2258cf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The rasterisation uses a ",
 StyleBox["RegionMember", "Input"],
 "-based subpixel test for anti-aliasing on thin/small countries."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"64997567-9647-439c-9b28-25145f7ac07f"],

Cell["2.2 Solve the diffusion equation", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"55039ec0-d071-4f03-b3de-94e24fe6e979"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Laplacian on a rectangle with Neumann boundary conditions is \
diagonalised by the cosine basis. Wolfram's built-in ",
 StyleBox["FourierDCT[\[CenterEllipsis], 2]", "Input"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["FourierDCT[\[CenterEllipsis], 3]", "Input"],
 " implement the DCT-II and its inverse in any number of dimensions with an \
orthonormal convention, so the full 2D spectrum is one call each. Expanding"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04cf3e5a-37d4-4181-9241-3cc824c9f102"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", 
    StyleBox["r",
     FontWeight->Bold], ",", " ", "t", ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{"m", ",", "n"}], ""], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[Rho]", "^"], 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", "n"}]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["e", 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
       RowBox[{"m", " ", "n"}]], " ", "t"}]], " ", 
    RowBox[{"cos", "(", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", " ", "m", " ", "x"}], 
      SubscriptBox["L", "x"]], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"cos", "(", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", " ", "n", " ", "y"}], 
      SubscriptBox["L", "y"]], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",\

 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"5da40588-ce36-4535-978a-2a5cedf705f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with eigenvalues ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", "n"}]], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       SuperscriptBox["m", "2"], 
       SubsuperscriptBox["L", "x", "2"]], "+", 
      FractionBox[
       SuperscriptBox["n", "2"], 
       SubsuperscriptBox["L", "y", "2"]]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "feafea95-709d-4187-847d-205ea1b7b6d4"],
 ", the density at any time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ec64a7d7-1ce8-45cc-97de-080c01e92a7c"],
 " is evaluated in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"O", "(", "N", " ", "Log", " ", "N", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "a9af71ed-3c7b-4181-973e-e6d2abb5c041"],
 " from the cached cosine coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox["\[Rho]", "^"], 
    RowBox[{"m", " ", "n"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "bdf5fe70-7d63-4ada-8acb-df86374de1ad"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ee119f60-e726-42fa-9e47-ee82a75251ec"],

Cell["2.3 Advect points through the velocity field", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"8a1dd4af-9279-4eec-a23c-0ad33e30fb7c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The velocity on the grid is computed by central differences on the current \
diffused grid and interpolated bilinearly at any query point. Each geographic \
point is integrated from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"t", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "01cc375a-f5be-4c51-830d-2bfc67af0854"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "\[Star]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "fa9e46bc-ff0f-4244-aca6-503ea2355303"],
 " using an explicit Runge\[Dash]Kutta scheme (",
 StyleBox["NDSolveValue[\[CenterEllipsis], Method -> \"ExplicitRungeKutta\"]",
   "Input"],
 ") with a 5th-order stepper, where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "\[Star]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "9e2d7ecb-b589-4212-aca7-ce37755950b5"],
 " is chosen from the decay constant of the slowest non-constant Fourier mode."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10ec9af4-32f8-4243-81e4-087ab56db013"],

Cell["2.4 Pre-smoothing", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e2260602-4bde-47fa-81ea-297652644dad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because polygon-rasterisation produces step functions, the initial velocity \
field is very stiff. We pre-smooth the density with a small Gaussian filter (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", "\[TildeTilde]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "e5eb0691-561f-418d-9d00-bec521d76870"],
 " cell), which is mathematically equivalent to starting the diffusion at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["t", "0"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "2"], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", "x", " ", 
     "\[CapitalDelta]", "y", "/", "2"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "c98aa1ea-ce87-4827-83a0-3bff17c6b846"],
 ". A small background floor (",
 StyleBox["MeanFloor", "Input"],
 ") is added to avoid division by zero inside zero-density cells."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"75e12eab-2f6d-4a1b-824a-2067c7581857"],

Cell["2.5 Snapshot-cached advection (the default Speed mode)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"72623ed9-a3ba-4ee6-9ebe-afb4d86cc562"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A naive implementation recomputes the full inverse DCT of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", 
    StyleBox["r",
     FontWeight->Bold], ",", " ", "t", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "0cd87023-7d2a-4292-ad3b-6ac2657ca0e3"],
 " at every RK sub-step of the advection ODE. With ~100+ sub-steps on a 192\
\[Times]384 grid this dominates wall-clock at ~320 s for a single world map. \
The package avoids it: at construction time we pre-compute a small (default \
60) set of geometrically-spaced snapshots of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "\[Rho]", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], "\[Rho]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "y"], "\[Rho]"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "a6591716-fd8d-4814-a38a-0af9975f2e6c"],
 ", spanning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"t", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "fa93087f-dcff-400e-a31f-57d29714d430"],
 " through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "\[Star]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "35c44431-871c-4bac-b405-a71541529f4b"],
 " with more samples packed near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"t", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "d7856a1a-4821-48c1-98e8-edb7a4d53691"],
 " where the fast Fourier modes collapse. During integration the RHS linearly \
interpolates between the two bracketing snapshots instead of doing a fresh \
inverse DCT. Median per-point agreement with the Quality solver is sub-pixel \
at rendering resolution and the full world pipeline drops from \
~5\[ThinSpace]min to ~45 s (~7\[Times] faster). Pass ",
 StyleBox["PerformanceGoal -> \"Quality\"", "Input"],
 " to any function that integrates points (",
 StyleBox["AdvectPoints", "Input"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["CartogramRun", "Input"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["WorldCartogram", "Input"],
 ") for the slower, bit-exact variant."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10c1721e-6a6f-4c73-9a04-0222361be6bf"],

Cell["3. The CartogramWL package", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"10e7a221-345d-408f-a174-d894c4c1b944"],

Cell["3.1 Loading", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e90a2ce5-4843-46a7-9f2b-2adee73346bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Clone the repository from GitHub and load the package directly from the ",
 StyleBox["CartogramWL/", "Input"],
 " directory. The package has zero external dependencies."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3ad88886-df73-4fa7-b063-0d5847310d2b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Get", "[", "\"\</path/to/wolfram/CartogramWL/CartogramWL.wl\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5f5e1d20-9a9e-479d-995a-26af48d454ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All public symbols are then available in the ",
 StyleBox["CartogramWL`", "Input"],
 " context:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c7821fb5-7df4-4f4d-a874-dcc91d332380"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Names", "[", "\"\<CartogramWL`*\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e4043f6b-7dd7-410a-a7d6-9a24fa231ad6"],

Cell["3.2 Low-level primitives", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"a283cea1-8dd2-4bf5-b3ff-1ebd14126da5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The algorithm is exposed as a handful of composable functions that all \
operate on a density array ",
 StyleBox["rho[[i, j]]", "Input"],
 " with row index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"i", " ", "\[LeftRightArrow]", " ", "y"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "87c8b1e6-6d58-438f-8ff7-9c27f9291d2c"],
 ", column index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"j", " ", "\[LeftRightArrow]", " ", "x"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "806d14af-2ac6-4bbe-850b-dd0a5a78b899"],
 " (NumPy convention) and a bounding box ",
 StyleBox["{xmin, ymin, xmax, ymax}", "Input"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"64555992-19e1-41c1-b1c6-7d4644b81d73"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solver", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DiffusionSolver", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"xmin", ",", " ", "ymin", ",", " ", "xmax", ",", " ", "ymax"}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rhoAtT", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DensityAt", "[", 
    RowBox[{"solver", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"newPts", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AdvectPoints", "[", 
    RowBox[{"solver", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", " ", "y1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"x2", ",", " ", "y2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6e20331b-e02b-4709-94cc-\
ff2f42c376e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One level up, ",
 StyleBox["Cartogram", "Input"],
 " bundles the pre-smoothing, mean floor, and ocean-preservation settings; ",
 StyleBox["CartogramRun", "Input"],
 " precomputes the deformed cell-centre grid (Speed mode by default, ~7\
\[Times] faster than Quality); ",
 StyleBox["CartogramTransform", "Input"],
 " maps arbitrary points through the deformation; ",
 StyleBox["CartogramTransformPolygon", "Input"],
 " additionally densifies long edges before the transform."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f7288a4c-45cc-48c8-88d6-602e831349f1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"cart", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Cartogram", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "bbox", ",", " ", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<MeanFloor\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BlurSigma\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1.5"}], ",", " ", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<SeaDensity\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<auto\>\""}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"cart", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CartogramRun", "[", 
    RowBox[{"cart", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PerformanceGoal", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Speed\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"newPoly", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CartogramTransformPolygon", "[", 
    RowBox[{"cart", ",", " ", "polyRing"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",Expressi\
onUUID->"7a73dd58-a443-4fae-a3f6-0cd74e901790"],

Cell["3.3 The one-liner: WorldCartogram", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"14795700-6e67-4f7c-a625-46a976309aaf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Most end users want \"given a metric, draw the world\". ",
 StyleBox["WorldCartogram", "Input"],
 " wraps the whole pipeline, reads polygons and values from ",
 StyleBox["CountryData", "Input"],
 ", and returns a two-panel ",
 StyleBox["GraphicsRow", "Input"],
 " (geographic + cartogram)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b89ea279-c4c9-4b30-b3f1-3e1472ad7c84"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"WorldCartogram", "[", "\"\<Population\>\"", "]"}], "          ", 
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"or", " ", "\"\<GDP\>\""}], ",", " ", "\"\<GDPPerCapita\>\"", ",",
     " ", "..."}], " ", "*)"}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"WorldCartogram", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<GDP\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ColorFunction\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "\"\<TemperatureMap\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"WorldCartogram", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<GDP\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Background\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Satellite\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"WorldCartogram", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<my metric\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<Germany\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "83."}], ",", " ", "..."}], 
     "|>"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"13ffa26c-d564-44fd-\
a265-187695f1747b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A complete option list is available via ",
 StyleBox["?WorldCartogram", "Input"],
 ". The most useful options are ",
 StyleBox["\"ColorFunction\"", "Input"],
 " (any ",
 StyleBox["ColorData[\[Ellipsis]]", "Input"],
 " gradient or a raw function on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"[", "0", ",", "1", "]"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "593807a9-c40a-4f7a-9bd5-5cd3a316d9ab"],
 "), ",
 StyleBox["\"Background\"", "Input"],
 " (",
 StyleBox["\"Flat\"", "Input"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["\"Satellite\"", "Input"],
 "), ",
 StyleBox["\"MissingCountries\"", "Input"],
 " (",
 StyleBox["\"Hide\"", "Input"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["\"ShowGrey\"", "Input"],
 "), ",
 StyleBox["\"BoundingBox\"", "Input"],
 " (useful for continent-scale maps), and ",
 StyleBox["PerformanceGoal", "Input"],
 " (",
 StyleBox["\"Speed\"", "Input"],
 " default, or ",
 StyleBox["\"Quality\"", "Input"],
 " for bit-exact output)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dfe19386-2a95-4040-9be7-201612d353b1"],

Cell["4. Built-in metrics", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"88b20532-8013-46d6-b937-9541bd3414ea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The four strings ",
 StyleBox["\"Population\"", "Input"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\"GDP\"", "Input"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\"GDPPerCapita\"", "Input"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\"PopulationDensity\"", "Input"],
 " are recognised directly and come with sensible defaults for the \
floor/ceiling that tame heavy-tailed outliers (Monaco on population density, \
Luxembourg on GDP per capita). The sections below show each of them in turn; \
every image on this page is produced by the literal one-line call shown next \
to it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b47ce213-9725-4004-b9fa-241b3b398d42"],

Cell["4.1 Population", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"83823bf7-d983-4c5e-921a-9b6250ca494b"],

Cell["\<\
The canonical cartogram: each country's area is made proportional to how many \
people live there. India and China together house ~36 % of humanity, so they \
swell enormously. Nigeria, Indonesia, Pakistan and Bangladesh together host \
nearly a billion more people across land areas that look small on a Mercator \
projection \[LongDash] all four bulge substantially. Russia (11 % of global \
land but 2 % of humanity), Canada, Australia, Mongolia and the Nordic \
countries collapse.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7723ff8-0523-496e-8a56-a2ce03758c26"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"WorldCartogram", "[", "\"\<Population\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",Expressi\
onUUID->"4067418c-611c-4e41-88dd-9a2e0ddbf7bb"],

