Cell["4.2 GDP", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"682eeea8-18de-4356-9f94-d94274f9fbff"],

Cell["\<\
Switching to gross domestic product (total value of goods and services \
produced in a year) rewards economic output rather than headcount. The United \
States, China, Japan, and the major western European economies dominate; \
sub-Saharan Africa and much of South Asia \[LongDash] densely populated but \
far poorer per head \[LongDash] shrink dramatically. This is the mirror image \
of the population cartogram wherever the two quantities diverge most: Japan \
(5\[ThinSpace]th largest economy, 11\[ThinSpace]th most populous) expands \
here but stays modestly sized in 4.1, while the Democratic Republic of the \
Congo does the opposite.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e85a6ea-9f00-48b7-b308-d9235e9d8f81"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"WorldCartogram", "[", "\"\<GDP\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"35ffd661-6121-4530-94c9-b2c4557de58d"],

